From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mobileshell: status bar: one indicator per connection, states of activation and failure
Description:
 The internet indicator showed the icon of the primary connection and,
 while any connection was being activated (mobile data included), a busy
 indicator in its place. With Wi-Fi connected and mobile data activating,
 the Wi-Fi icon turned into a spinner that told nothing about the
 connection it stood for.
 .
 The status bar now has a fixed indicator per connection, each shown only
 when it matters: the signal of every SIM; the Wi-Fi signal while Wi-Fi is
 connected or connecting; the hotspot while it is active; the airplane
 icon in place of the signals in airplane mode. There is no generic
 internet icon and no busy indicator; wired and USB connections have no
 indicator.
 .
 The SIM used for mobile data carries the network type (5G, LTE, H+, E,
 ...) left of its signal while mobile data is connected. While mobile data
 or Wi-Fi is being activated, the network type or the Wi-Fi icon pulses,
 after a minute in the negative color (still trying, not working yet).
 After a failed activation a red cross replaces the network type, or sits
 at the bottom right of the Wi-Fi icon, until the connection is up or the
 user disables and enables mobile data or Wi-Fi; retries of
 NetworkManager do not bring the pulsing back. Mobile data disabled, the
 SIM not used for mobile data, Wi-Fi disabled or not connecting: nothing.
 .
 Pulsing: opacity from invisible to visible, 1 s fade in (sine), 0.2 s
 visible, 1 s fade out, 0.2 s invisible, one phase for all indicators
 (IndicatorPulse); the space of the indicator stays reserved. The
 animation runs only while an indicator pulses and a screen is on (DPMS);
 with animations disabled the indicator is shown half transparent.
 .
 Needs the plasma-nm libraries with WirelessStatus.wifiState/
 wifiSignalStrength and CellularModem.mobileDataState/networkType.
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-2.0-or-later, LGPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched files; new files GPL-2.0-or-later)
